+# Experimental JEV tiered storage
+
+Disabled by default. `--tiered-pack PATH` adds a lossy sidecar for a single-shard
+model's Q4_K expert slices. Hot slices still come from the original GGUF. Cold
+slices expand into the Q4_K buffers the CPU kernels already consume. No changes
+to llama.cpp, routing overrides, or expert dropping.
+
+The JEVTIER1 header stores source file size, sampled FNV-1a fingerprint and extent
+count. Little-endian 40-byte entries store source offset, pack offset, raw length,
+stored length and codec id. Pack extents are 4096-aligned. Entries are validated
+against discovered Q4_K expert geometry. The fingerprint guards accidental model
+mismatches, not malicious substitution; the builder records full source SHA256.
+
+Codec 1 retains a Q4_K block's 16 metadata bytes, selects one of 16 four-value
+nibble codebooks, and stores 256 two-bit indices: 81 bytes instead of 144. Decoding
+restores quantized nibbles, NOT the original cold weights. Hot weights stay exact.
+SSSE3 accelerates expansion on supported x86 CPUs; other targets use scalar code.
+
+SSD transfers shrink, but expanded cache size and CPU weight traffic do not. The
+original GGUF is still required, so the sidecar adds installed disk usage. This
+is not a compact replacement GGUF or the Flash-MoE file format.
+
+Expert read-byte counters include source and sidecar reads. A shutdown diagnostic
+reports sidecar bytes and summed expansion lane-seconds. Expansion contributes to
+wall time but not reader syscall time. Speculative byte counts still describe
+logical expanded slices. Parallel lane-seconds are not serial wall time.
+
+`--choices-only --ppl-list FILE --ppl-choices A,B` scores already-rendered chat
+prompts. Special tokens are parsed; only last-position logits are requested.
+Labels must be single tokens. No text perplexity is computed. Probabilities are
+uncalibrated. Many prompts share one loaded process, but prefixes are not batched
+together. Ordinary perplexity mode is unchanged.
+
+The parent JEV workspace contains the builder, tests and scoring adapter under
+`scripts/tiered/`, with results in `docs/TIERED-STORAGE-RESULT.md`. Both measured
+quantization policies failed their quality gate and remain experimental.
